  "id": "comparative-cognition",
  "term": "comparative cognition",
  "definition": "Comparative cognition is the study of thinking abilities across species, especially how nonhuman animals perform cognitive processes such as understanding similarities, analogies, and same/different relations. It examines the extent to which abilities often associated with human advanced cognition also appear in other species.",
